# Build artifacts
fortran/*.so
fortran/*.o
*.mod
fortran/_sacsma_patched/

# Extracted from external/snow17/test_cases/ex1.tgz at test time
external/snow17/test_cases/ex1/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/

# CAMELS data: downloaded via data/download_camels.sh, not committed
# (the forcing+flow archive alone is ~3.4GB, ~14GB extracted). Ignore
# everything under data/camels/ except the one small, human-readable,
# reproducible-from-a-fixed-seed reference worth keeping in the repo:
# selected_basins.csv (which basins we used, and why -- frac_snow etc).
# basin_attributes.npz is regenerated by data/build_attributes.py in
# seconds from the (untracked, re-downloadable) attribute text files --
# not tracked despite being small, since it's binary/undiffable and
# fully reproducible.
data/camels/*
!data/camels/selected_basins.csv

# src/train.py's default output_dir is timestamped
# (results/runs/<model>_<split>_<timestamp>/) -- exploratory runs
# shouldn't accumulate in git. One canonical, reproducible reference run
# is kept, plus its reproduction under the current forward-mode coupling
# (results/README.md). Previously also kept a
# 3-year pilot run and (earlier still) two benchmark_lstm run dirs --
# both removed along with the code/results they belonged to; see
# notes/logs.md.
results/runs/*
!results/runs/model_9yrs_spatial/
!results/runs/model_9yrs_spatial_fwdmode/
# Hydra's own job-logging artifacts (.hydra/, train.log) -- present when
# a run went through cli()'s @hydra.main path rather than run_training()
# called directly; not part of the run's actual content (config.yaml/
# checkpoint.pt/history.json already capture everything reproducible).
results/runs/*/.hydra/
results/runs/*/train.log
results/predictions/

# Periodic resume checkpoints (model + optimizer state, every
# train.checkpoint_every epochs) -- a local training convenience, not a
# result artifact; committing ~30 of these per canonical run would be
# pure binary bloat. checkpoint.pt (final) and test_predictions.json
# stay tracked in the canonical runs above -- only this subdirectory is excluded.
results/runs/*/checkpoints/

# Hydra's own bookkeeping (config.yaml, overrides.yaml, hydra.yaml,
# <job>.log) nests inside each run's output_dir (configs/config.yaml's
# hydra.run.dir) -- ignored wherever a run happens to land, as a
# safety net in case output_dir is ever overridden to somewhere untracked.
.hydra/
*.log

# tesseract_core.Tesseract.from_tesseract_api()'s LocalClient creates one
# of these per client (so two per CoupledNWSStack -- snow17 + sacsma) via
# tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="tesseract_output_") whenever output_path isn't
# passed explicitly (every call site in this repo). Never cleaned up by
# the SDK itself, and lands in the repo root rather than /tmp if $TMPDIR
# is pointed here -- see chat log / notes/logs.md for the investigation.
tesseract_output_*/

# PyTorch's TorchInductor compiled-kernel cache (torch._inductor) --
# same tempfile.gettempdir() root cause as tesseract_output_* above, not
# anything this repo requests explicitly (no torch.compile() call site
# exists here). Confirms $TMPDIR is pointed at this repo rather than
# /tmp in this environment -- worth fixing at the shell/env level, not
# just gitignoring, since it's the same cause behind both directories.
torchinductor_*/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.vscode/

# results/animate_training.py simulation cache (regenerated in ~20s)
results/.animate_cache.npz
